# A video in a page: its first picture is laid out with the page, and each
# frame after it is painted alone, where the page put it — a frame of video
# costs the player's rectangle, not the window. Needs the machine's video
# decoder. The frame is painted when a pixel is read, as the window paints
# when it draws; the colours are exact, as VP9's decoding is, and the
# picture is scaled smoothly (bilinear), as browsers scale video.
require-video-hardware
resize 640 400
open video.html
advance 10 5
assert-title Video playing
advance 100
assert-pixel 60 120 #402a02
mark
advance 100
assert-pixel 60 120 #452105
advance 100
assert-pixel 60 120 #400000
advance 100
assert-pixel 60 120 #25013f
assert-video-paints 3
assert-paints 0
assert-pixel 600 120 #222244
